==Finnish==
{{wikipedia|lang=fi|norsut}}

===Etymology===
Originally synonym of {{m|fi|mursu||walrus}} <ref>Kaisa Häkkinen: "Mursun ja norsun jäljillä", Virittäjä 4/2007 pp. 482–500</ref>, which is a loan from Northern Sami {{m|se|morša||walrus}}. Centuries ago, elephant was known in Finland only from stories for being a big, thick-skinned animal with handsome tusks, hence the initial confusion. The meanings differentiated around 18th century.

